let NEWS_DATE="Nov 4, 2026";
let NEWS=[
 {"k":"Economy","d":"Nov 4","h":"Democrats projected to win the House and Senate, and stock futures slip","w":"TV networks projected that Democrats will take control of both chambers of Congress after Tuesday's midterm elections. Overnight, S&P 500 futures fell about 0.5% and Nasdaq futures about 0.9%, while the dollar weakened.","m":"A split government, with a Republican president and a Democratic Congress, usually means fewer big new laws. Analysts said a narrow Democratic win was largely expected, and that tech fell more on worries about tighter rules for Big Tech and AI. UBS still expects the push to loosen bank rules to continue.","a":"Interviewers like to ask how politics moves markets. A clean answer: markets hate uncertainty more than either party, so once results are clear, deal and IPO activity can pick up. Name one sector exposed to policy, like tech regulation or bank capital rules.","s":[["Reuters via Yahoo Finance","https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/us-stock-futures-dip-investors-010842458.html"],["Reuters via Yahoo Finance (analysts)","https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/analysts-react-us-midterm-election-025738421.html"],["CNBC live","https://www.cnbc.com/2026/11/03/midterm-elections-2026-live-updates.html"]]},
 {"k":"Markets","d":"Nov 3","h":"AMD's sales jump 45% and it forecasts about $17 billion next quarter","w":"AMD reported third-quarter revenue of $13.4 billion, up 45% from a year earlier, with record data center sales of $8.5 billion, nearly double last year. It guided fourth-quarter revenue to about $17 billion, and the stock jumped in after-hours trading.","m":"After weeks of doubts about AI spending, a chipmaker forecasting 66% growth next quarter is a sign the AI build-out is still running hot. It helped lift Asian tech stocks overnight.","a":"Show you know guidance often matters more than the quarter itself. The stock trades on what investors expect next, so a big forecast above estimates can move the price more than a small beat on past results.","s":[["AMD earnings release (SEC)","https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/0000002488/000000248826000188/q32026991.htm"],["Yahoo Finance","https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/stock-market-today-nov-3-230359079.html"]]},
 {"k":"Markets","d":"Nov 3","h":"Chips lift the Nasdaq 0.8% while Apple drags the Dow lower","w":"The Nasdaq rose 0.83% to 25,372 and the S&P 500 gained 0.36% to 7,569 as Nvidia, Broadcom and other chip stocks bounced. The Dow fell 0.38% to 51,787 as Apple slid 1.9% on a weaker profit-margin forecast tied to rising memory chip costs.","m":"The 10-year Treasury yield climbed to about 4.95%, close to 5%, which makes stocks look pricier next to safe bonds. Tech was the best of the S&P 500's 11 sectors, up 1.31%.","a":"Know why one stock can move the Dow so much: the Dow is price-weighted, so a high-priced stock like Apple counts more than a cheaper one, no matter how big each company is. The S&P 500 is weighted by market value instead.","s":[["Yahoo Finance","https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/stock-market-today-nov-3-230359079.html"],["Avalon Capital Research","https://avaloncapitalresearch.substack.com/p/closing-bell-chipmakers-lift-nasdaq"]]},
 {"k":"Banks","d":"Nov 3","h":"The Anthropic IPO could be the \"swing vote\" for big banks this quarter","w":"Anthropic's stock market debut could come as soon as Nov. 16, and all five of the largest U.S. banks are working on it. Evercore estimates the fees could add about 0.8% to the banks' fourth-quarter profits, with Goldman Sachs, Morgan Stanley and Citi gaining the most.","m":"Bank stocks need a boost: global investment banking activity fell 25% from a year earlier in October, as rising rates slowed deals and trading. At a Hong Kong summit, Goldman's David Solomon said good companies can still raise plenty of money, and Morgan Stanley's Ted Pick called AI investment the \"second inning of a nine-inning game.\"","a":"Be ready to explain how banks make money on an IPO: they underwrite the deal, buying the shares and reselling them to investors, and keep a fee called the gross spread. Bigger IPOs mean bigger fees, which is why one deal can move a quarter.","s":[["Yahoo Finance","https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/article/why-the-anthropic-ipo-could-be-the-swing-vote-for-wall-street-bank-stocks-172030065.html"]]},
 {"k":"PE","d":"Nov 3","h":"Apollo posts a $1.1 billion loss on paper, but its core fee business grows 23%","w":"Private markets giant Apollo reported a third-quarter GAAP net loss of $1.1 billion, mostly from mark-to-market losses at its retirement business as interest rates rose. Its fee-related earnings, the steady management fees, rose 23% to $802 million, and assets reached $1.07 trillion.","m":"Apollo's stock fell about 4.9% to $113.56. Investors watch fee earnings most because they recur, but the loss shows how higher rates hit firms that own big insurance companies, like Apollo's Athene.","a":"Great example for the question \"why do bond values fall when rates rise?\" Older bonds pay less than new ones, so their prices drop. Also know the difference between GAAP net income and fee-related earnings at an asset manager.","s":[["Apollo earnings release (SEC)","https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/0001858681/000185868126000063/agmearningsrelease3q2026.htm"],["Avalon Capital Research","https://avaloncapitalresearch.substack.com/p/closing-bell-chipmakers-lift-nasdaq"]]},
 {"k":"Markets","d":"Nov 3","h":"Fiserv soars 12%, while Shopify and Gartner sink after earnings","w":"Payments company Fiserv jumped about 12.5% to $58.40 after beating forecasts and raising its cost-savings targets. Shopify fell about 8.7% after its first revenue miss in four years, and research firm Gartner dropped about 13% on slower subscription growth.","m":"The moves show how much is riding on each report. Stocks with high expectations get punished for small misses, while beaten-down stocks can rally hard on decent news.","a":"Use this for \"priced for perfection.\" A stock trading at a high multiple already assumes great growth, so even a small miss can cut the multiple and the price at the same time.","s":[["Yahoo Finance","https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/stock-market-today-nov-3-230359079.html"],["Avalon Capital Research","https://avaloncapitalresearch.substack.com/p/closing-bell-chipmakers-lift-nasdaq"],["Stocktitan","https://www.stocktitan.net/articles/stock-market-today-live-november-3-2026"]]},
 {"k":"Economy","d":"Nov 3","h":"Job openings hold near 7.5 million ahead of Friday's jobs report","w":"U.S. job openings were roughly unchanged at about 7.5 million in September, above the 7.1 million forecast. Quits rose to 3.4 million and hires held at 5.4 million.","m":"More people quitting usually means workers feel confident and can push for raises, which can keep inflation up. Friday's October jobs report is expected to show about 63,000 new jobs.","a":"Know the quits rate: it is a signal of wage pressure. The Fed watches it because rising wages can feed inflation, which is why a strong labor market can mean higher rates.","s":[["Avalon Capital Research","https://avaloncapitalresearch.substack.com/p/closing-bell-chipmakers-lift-nasdaq"],["Investing.com","https://ph.investing.com/news/stock-market-news/weekly-economic-outlook-payrolls-and-fed-speakers-in-focus-93CH-2668065"]]},
 {"k":"Deals","d":"Nov 3","h":"Clarivate jumps about 25% after closing a $488 million sale early","w":"Data company Clarivate closed the sale of its life sciences and healthcare unit early, on Oct. 6, for about $488 million in net cash. It plans to use the money to cut debt and now focuses on two businesses, academic research tools and patents.","m":"Selling a slower unit and paying down debt is a classic fix for a company with too much leverage. Clarivate's shares surged as investors cheered the cleaner, less risky business.","a":"Practice the divestiture logic: selling a unit and repaying debt lowers leverage and interest costs. If the unit sold at a higher multiple than the whole company trades at, the sale can add value for shareholders.","s":[["Clarivate earnings release (SEC)","https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/0001764046/000176404626000125/ex991q32026earningsrelease.htm"],["Stocktitan","https://www.stocktitan.net/articles/stock-market-today-live-november-3-2026"]]},
 {"k":"Banks","d":"Nov 2","h":"Fed survey: banks made it harder to borrow for the first time in a year","w":"A Federal Reserve survey of loan officers found U.S. banks broadly tightened their lending standards in the third quarter, ending four straight quarters of easing. Demand for loans also weakened in most categories.","m":"Tighter bank lending slows the economy, which is part of what the Fed wants as it fights inflation. It also makes buyouts harder to finance, giving private credit funds more room to lend instead.","a":"Connect the dots for a PE interview: when banks pull back, LBOs get less debt or pay more for it, so buyers must put in more equity, and returns (IRR) fall unless they pay a lower price.","s":[["Yahoo Finance","https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/article/why-the-anthropic-ipo-could-be-the-swing-vote-for-wall-street-bank-stocks-172030065.html"]]},
 {"k":"Deals","d":"Nov 2","h":"Marvell agrees to buy Lumentum for about $115 billion in stock, and both shares fall","w":"Chipmaker Marvell agreed to buy Lumentum, which makes lasers and other optical parts for AI data centers, in an all-stock deal valued at about $115 billion. Lumentum owners get 4.5 Marvell shares per share, and they would own about 33% of the combined company.","m":"It is one of the biggest tech deals ever and a large bet that data centers will move data with light. Both stocks dropped, with Marvell closing down about 13% and Lumentum about 19%, as investors worried about the price and the wait, since closing is not expected until the first half of 2028.","a":"Great stock-deal example. The $1,132 per share headline used Oct 28 prices, but the 4.5 share ratio is fixed, so the value moves with Marvell's stock. At Monday's $171.11 Marvell close, 4.5 shares are worth about $770.","s":[["Yahoo Finance","https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/marvell-strikes-115b-deal-acquire-124300132.html"],["CBS News","https://www.cbsnews.com/news/marvell-lumentum-acquisition-ai-connectivity/"],["Marvell 8-K via Stocktitan","https://www.stocktitan.net/sec-filings/MRVL/8-k-marvell-technology-inc-reports-material-event-7df547335b18.html"],["Stocktitan live","https://www.stocktitan.net/articles/stock-market-today-live-november-2-2026"]]},
 {"k":"Deals","d":"Nov 2","h":"EVgo jumps about 47% after its controlling owner LS Power offers $2 a share","w":"LS Power, which already holds about 56% of the voting power at electric-car charging company EVgo, proposed buying the public shares it does not own for $2.00 each in cash. The offer is non-binding, and EVgo's board formed a special committee to review it.","m":"This would take EVgo private, but it is not a signed deal yet. The stock's surge shows investors expect a sale, and possibly a better price.","a":"Explain why a special committee matters. When the buyer already controls the company, independent directors negotiate for the small shareholders, because the controlling owner sits on both sides of the deal.","s":[["Stocktitan","https://www.stocktitan.net/news/EVGO/e-vgo-confirms-receipt-of-unsolicited-and-non-binding-take-private-erxkkelel9p6.html"],["Stocktitan live","https://www.stocktitan.net/articles/stock-market-today-live-november-2-2026"]]},
 {"k":"Markets","d":"Nov 2","h":"Oracle raises $20 billion for AI spending, and its stock falls about 9%","w":"Oracle announced a $20 billion capital raise, split between about $10 billion of bonds and a similar amount of stock. Alphabet and Microsoft are also selling debt to pay for AI, including a reported 6 billion euro bond sale by Alphabet.","m":"Big tech used to pay for growth with its own cash. Now the AI build-out is so costly that even giants are tapping bond and stock markets, which gives capital markets bankers plenty of work but makes investors question the payoff.","a":"Explain debt vs. equity financing: bonds add interest payments and leverage, while new shares add no interest but dilute current owners. That dilution is one reason a stock can fall on a raise.","s":[["Yahoo Finance","https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/live/stock-market-today-monday-november-2-dow-sp-500-nasdaq-091835095.html"],["Motley Fool","https://www.fool.com/coverage/stock-market-today/2026/11/02/stock-market-midday-nov-2-stocks-rally-as-oil-prices-tumble-on-diplomatic-hopes/"]]},
 {"k":"Deals","d":"Nov 2","h":"Blackstone-led group pays $3.1 billion for 49.9% of Mitsubishi's LNG Canada unit","w":"Blackstone and four Canadian pension investors, including CPP Investments and OMERS, agreed to pay US$3.1 billion for a 49.9% non-controlling stake in a Mitsubishi unit. That unit holds Mitsubishi's 15% interest in LNG Canada, the country's first liquefied natural gas export plant.","m":"Mitsubishi raises cash but keeps control and its full share of the plant's gas. Investors get a stake in a long-life energy asset, the kind that pension funds like for steady income.","a":"This is a minority stake sale, a way to free up cash without selling the asset. Do the math: $3.1 billion for 49.9% implies about $6.2 billion for the whole unit.","s":[["Canadian Press via BNN Bloomberg","https://bnnbloomberg.ca/business/company-news/2026/11/02/blackstone-led-group-buys-into-mitsubishi-subsidiary-that-holds-lng-canada-stake"]]},
 {"k":"Economy","d":"Oct 30","h":"Two Fed officials say interest rates need to go higher, and soon","w":"St. Louis Fed President Alberto Musalem said inflation is too high and spread across the economy, so more rate increases will be needed soon. Richmond Fed President Tom Barkin agreed rates should rise given strong demand, saying the only real question is how fast.","m":"Their comments come days after the Fed held rates in a split vote, and after September PCE inflation rose to 3.6% with Q3 growth at 3.4%. Traders now lean toward a December hike, which would make borrowing more expensive for companies and buyout firms.","a":"Be ready to explain why the Fed raises rates when inflation is high: higher rates cool spending and borrowing. For PE, higher rates mean pricier LBO debt, so firms can borrow less and must pay lower multiples to hit their target returns.","s":[["AOL","https://www.aol.com/articles/rates-higher-2-fed-members-170145000.html"],["Yahoo Finance","https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/live/stock-market-today-friday-october-30-dow-sp-500-nasdaq-amazon-intel-131609630.html"]]}
];
